<node id="1218173" title="Re^2: Any downsides to this slurp idiom?" created="2018-07-09 12:46:08" updated="2018-07-09 12:46:08" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="832495">choroba</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">Note that localizing @ARGV could be [http://blogs.perl.org/users/book/2018/07/a-widespread-and-broken-perl-idiom.html|not enough] (because &lt;c&gt;eof(ARGV)&lt;/c&gt; might remain true). So,
&lt;c&gt;
my $data = do { local ( *ARGV, $/ ); @ARGV = ("$file"); &lt;&gt; };
&lt;/c&gt;&lt;P&gt;

